<title>USA: Sequa Corp Q4 posts lower net after charge.</title>
<headline>Sequa Corp Q4 posts lower net after charge.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>(Amounts in thousands, except per share)</p>
<p>				 Three Months	    Full Year</p>
<p>				1996	1995	 1996	 1995</p>
<p> Sales		   $380,744  $376,054 $1,459,029 $1,414,139</p>
<p> Net income		11,845    14,811	9,187	8,779</p>
<p> Net income		  1.12	1.42	  .61	  .57</p>
<p>NOTE: 1996 Q4 includes litigation expenses of $6.3 million.</p>
<p>1995 Q4 includes a $6.5 million pretax gain on the sale of the Kollsman division, which also added $20.2 million in sales for the period.</p>
<p>1996 year includes a charge of $369,000, or $0.04 a share, from retirement of debt, a $2.5 million restructuring charge related to auxiliary press equipment supplier, and $33 million of expenses related to litigation against the Pratt &amp; Whitney unit of United Technologies Corp.</p>
<p>1995 year includes $97.3 million in sales from Kollsman division, which added $12.9 million in operating income.</p>
</text>
